            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>There is described a method of processing a biological sample selected from sputum, nasal mucous, nasal discharge, an oropharyngeal swab sample, bronco alveolar lavage, bronchial washings, and nasopharyngeal swab sample, the method comprising contacting the biological sample with a composition comprising at least one degradative enzyme and a detergent, and optionally, a buffer and/or a divalent cation chelator.</p>
